// Schools, school districts and general hospitals located inside each of the 30
// neighborhoods in ./neighborhoods.js. STATIC DATA, generated by a script from
// official sources -- do not hand-edit; regenerate instead.
//
// FAIR HOUSING -- non-negotiable, same rule as neighborhoods.js. This file holds
// NAMES, GRADE SPANS, PUBLIC/CHARTER and DISTRICT NUMBERS only. No ratings,
// test scores, rankings, enrolment, demographics or quality language of any
// kind, and nothing of that sort may be added. The district number is a fact
// about where the lines are drawn, not a judgement.
//
// SOURCES (all official, all downloaded 2026-10-21):
//   Schools: NYC Department of Education, "School Point Locations" (NYC Open
//     Data jfju-ynrr), https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/jfju-ynrr: the
//     SchoolPoints_APS_2024_08_28 shapefile, DOE's own School Search base
//     layer for the 2024-25 school year (the newest school-location file with
//     coordinates on NYC Open Data, re-checked 2026-10-21; DOE's live LCGMS
//     directory is not published as a file). Downloaded 2026-10-21T19:22Z.
//     That file carries name, location code, geographic district and point
//     only, so: public/charter is read from the ATS code (district 84 =
//     charter); grade spans come from DOE's "2019 - 2020 School Locations"
//     table (NYC Open Data wg9x-4ke6, https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/wg9x-4ke6,
//     downloaded 2026-10-21T16:45Z) matched by location code, and are absent
//     for schools opened since (Pre-K Centers show "PK", which is their name);
//     where the shapefile cuts a name at 50 characters the 2019-20 full name
//     is used. Excluded as not being schools with regular enrolment: Alternate
//     Learning Centers (ATS district 88), District 79 alternative programs,
//     home- and hospital-instruction entries, DOE offices and stray program /
//     daycare records (ATS 33, 64, 93).
//   School district boundaries: NYC Department of City Planning, "School
//     Districts" (NYC Open Data 8ugf-3d8u), https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/8ugf-3d8u,
//     downloaded 2026-10-21T16:43Z.
//   Hospitals: NYS Department of Health, "Health Facility General Information"
//     (health.data.ny.gov vn5v-hh5r) joined to "Health Facility Certification
//     Information" (2g9y-7kqm); a general hospital = an Article 28 hospital
//     certified for Medical / Surgical beds. Downloaded 2026-10-21T16:43Z.
//     Clinics, extension clinics, psychiatric-only and specialty hospitals
//     without medical/surgical beds are excluded.
//   Neighborhood boundaries: NYC Department of City Planning, "2020
//     Neighborhood Tabulation Areas (NTAs)" (NYC Open Data 9nt8-h7nd),
//     https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/9nt8-h7nd, downloaded 2026-10-21T16:43Z,
//     for 16 neighborhoods. The other 14 use street polygons (below) whose
//     corners sit on named-street intersections from OpenStreetMap
//     (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL; fetched 2026-10-21 via Overpass).
//
// METHOD. Each entry's `boundary` says which shape was used:
//   "nta"     -- the union of the 2020 NTAs listed under `ntas`.
//   "streets" -- a polygon drawn along the streets listed under `streets`,
//                used where the NTA is shared with another of our neighborhoods
//                (Carroll Gardens / Cobble Hill / Gowanus share one NTA, as do
//                DUMBO / Downtown Brooklyn) or is noticeably wider than the
//                neighborhood (Flatbush-Ditmas Park, Long Island City, Chelsea,
//                Murray Hill, Financial District, Upper East Side, Astoria,
//                Williamsburg, Harlem). On these entries `ntas` lists the NTAs
//                the polygon was carved from, for reference only.
// A school or hospital is "in" a neighborhood when its point lies inside that
// shape. `districts` is the share of the neighborhood's AREA that falls in each
// Community School District; `primary_district` is the largest share and
// `other_districts` any others covering 15% or more.
//
// School assignment depends on the exact address, which is why the UI links
// to the city's own school search rather than implying any zoning here.

